      "writtenOn": "2023-01-05T11:24:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately, [`DiceHash`](http://cs/android/external/open-dice/src/boringssl_hash_kdf_ops.c?l\u003d28) ignores the context so we can\u0027t use it to hash both kernel and ramdisk into a single `code_hash` so will need to find a way to call BSSL\u0027s `SHA*` functions from Rust.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 30,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 30,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "61c1812172e5263d7237d0ec7678350fdbb776bd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0136470f_2c0d0a52",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/dice.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 30,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059815
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-05T14:33:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So you want to compute `hash(concat(code, ramdisk))`? Doesn\u0027t that ignore where the `code` ends and `ramdisk` begins? Shouldn\u0027t we compute `hash(concat(hash(code), hash(ramdisk)))` or something like that? Does the BCC spec say something about this?",
      "parentUuid": "ec24ab85_74841b64",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 30,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 30,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "61c1812172e5263d7237d0ec7678350fdbb776bd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a0a05a2e_4901c051",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/dice.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 30,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-05T18:07:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The spec [describes](https://pigweed.googlesource.com/open-dice/+/HEAD/docs/specification.md#input-values) the code input as being \"computed by hashing the target code\" which I interpret to include the ramdisk, not just the kernel.\n\nOnce we have the AVB code in, we should be computing\n```\nhash(concat(hash(kernel), hash(ramdisk)))\n```\nas `hash(kernel)` and `hash(ramdisk)` can be directly extracted from the VBMeta.\n\nAlternatively, we\u0027ll use the AVB digests i.e.\n```\nhash(concat(hash(vbmeta_kernel), hash(vbmeta_ramdisk)))\n```\nwhere `vbmeta_X` contains `hash(X)` see this [other comment](https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Virtualization/+/2377172/comment/d405f6eb_c9be7766/).\n\nFor now, are you suggesting I use\n```\nlet mut hashes \u003d [0; HASH_SIZE * 2];\nhashes[..HASH_SIZE] \u003d hash(kernel)?;\nhashes[HASH_SIZE..] \u003d hash(ramdisk)?;\nlet code_hash \u003d hash(hashes)?;\n```\n?",
      "parentUuid": "0136470f_2c0d0a52",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 30,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 30,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "61c1812172e5263d7237d0ec7678350fdbb776bd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7c7c59c6_eb0e31da",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/dice.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 30,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059815
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-05T18:35:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, that\u0027s an interesting point - should the properties of vbmeta be captured in the hash? I don\u0027t think so, as ultimately we only care about the state of memory before entering the next stage. So either of your suggestions should be fine, but maybe we can have a look at the bootloader and align with it?",
      "parentUuid": "a0a05a2e_4901c051",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 30,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 30,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "61c1812172e5263d7237d0ec7678350fdbb776bd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d405f6eb_c9be7766",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/dice.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 34,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-05T11:40:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "we must have calculated this for the verified boot. how can we reuse that?\n\nor can \u0027code\u0027 be the signature of the kernel, not the kernel itself?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 34,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 34,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "61c1812172e5263d7237d0ec7678350fdbb776bd",
